  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "If you log in to the VRChat SDK with a different account than the one you're signed in to in VR Chat, test builds don't appear in the \"Other\" tab.\n\nMy use case for this is that I occasionally do avatar re-texture commissions, and every so often, my client needs help uploading their avatar, usually because they struggle to set up the SDK on their own computer or aren't familiar enough with Unity to do it on their own, so they will allow me to log in to their account in the SDK so I can upload it.\n\nBut after this, since I am signed in to my own account in VR Chat, I can't see any further test builds, so it's a bit more trouble to iterate and improve the avatar when doing some final fixes. The workaround I found is to create and export a Unity Package and recreate the project in another instance with my personal account to iterate, however, this is quite clunky, and it would be a great quality of life improvement just to be able to see test avatars from multiple accounts.",
